## Original Content
Voters in at least six states will soon decide ballot measures related to voter ID — the largest number of voter ID measures in a single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states.

## Summary
Voters in at least six states will decide on voter ID ballot measures this year, which is the largest number of such measures in a single year. The tally includes three prominent swing states.

## Key Points
- At least six states will have voter ID ballot measures this year.
- This represents the highest number of voter ID measures in a single year.
- The measures include three key swing states.


